doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20077673
keywords:
  - Riemann zeta function
  - prime number theory
  - Bogomolny-Keating conjecture
  - computational number theory
  - experimental mathematics
  - pair correlation statistics
abstract: >-
  Exploratory numerical study of prime-dependent corrections to
  zeta zero spacing statistics. Observes empirical alignment with
  the Bogomolny-Keating (1996) amplitude prediction across three
  independent Odlyzko datasets (r varies: 0.45–0.68 (dataset-dependent)). Not a confirmed
  theorem. Not a proof of the Riemann Hypothesis. Independent
  replication required.
